This one hits different, for the last couple of months i've been waging an internal battle around vibe coding and ai assisted coding.

I think to understand my point once must understand the context behind it.

I graduated in 2023 from a bachelors degree in data science and AI. I started coding at 13, back thne just HTML, CSS, PHP, JS anmd some C

I love programming, I love the craft behind it, thecraftmanship, honing one's skills over years of experience and learning what works and what doesnt. Making mistakes etc

As vibe coding started trending this created two alternative realities: one where executiuves think that programming is dead, and one where the frontline workers (programmersm, and engineers) started adopting AI.

We saw different levels of adopiton for AI. No AI<--------> Vibe coding

